§ T14 severity-CLI
  new @ parser/semantic.odin : Sem_Mode + Sem_Severity + Sem_Code + Sem_Diag
  severity-table ← Q2-settled :
    dup-morph   = always-E
    order       = W→E@strict
    unknown     = W→E@strict
    slot-arity  = W@lint ; E@default+strict
    evidence    = W-always
    compound    = I-always
    permissive  = W@default ; E@strict-parse
  new @ parser/main.odin : --lint --strict --strict-parse --verbose
  exit-code : any-E @ default+strict ; any-W @ strict ; never-fail @ lint
  ★ found bug : collapse_morpheme_chain pre-emptive recursion ⇒ double-append
    fix : remove `_ = collapse(lhs, r)` ; walk-child-recursion handles descent
  test : tests/test_severity_modes.py ~200-LOC ; 22 assertions

§ T15 permissive-tagging
  13 fixtures carry `# permissive: true` header-line
  discover_permissive() reads headers ← no-hardcoded-set drift
  semantic detections @ check_permissive_accept :
    Function_Def.text-empty        → anon fn
    Type_Def|Enum_Def.text-empty   → anon type
    node.meta-starts-with(. | @)   → trailing-op drop (parser-marked)
    Directive.modal ≠ Invalid ∧ empty-payload → bare modal
  parser changes :
    parse_postfix .Dot no-ident → lhs.meta = "."
    parse_postfix .At no-target → lhs.meta = "@"
    parse_statement NL/EOF/Dedent → early-exit only-if no-slot-prefix-consumed
    parse_function_def / parse_type_def → clean empty-name for anon
    walk() preserves node.meta across n^ = collapsed^ copy
  coverage :
    6 direct detections via Permissive_Accept code
    2 indirect via dup-morpheme (always-E ⇒ exit-1 any-non-lint mode)
    5 gaps documented (c01 c02 s02 t02 p04)
  test : tests/test_permissive_accept.py ; 13/13 tagged ; 8 must-fail

